Subject: [PATCH 07/59] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS fix round (track site): two edge-bff
 sites on one database, the start-up, the background loops

- EDGE_SITE (beta, the default, or live); config.validate refuses live without EDGE_MULTIUSER, the beta with it (outside
  EDGE_ENVIRONMENT=local), an AI loop on live, and the log email mode with the switch on outside local (R2-26).
- Per-loop switches (EDGE_AI_WORKER_ENABLED: beta only by default; EDGE_BACKTEST_LOOP_ENABLED;
  EDGE_HOUSEKEEPING_ENABLED), all parsed with switch_of, as EDGE_WORKER_ENABLED and EDGE_EMAIL_ENABLED now (R2-36).
- Each site claims only its own queued rows (store.claim, BacktestStore claim/reap/prune by site; R2-7, R2-13, R2-23,
  R2-38); the switch-off resolver accepts only sessions without an account (R2-1); the seed copies
  EDGE_PASSWORD_VERIFIER only over its own copy (R2-2).
- The live site never holds a beta-only capability (the Monitor and admin tabs, the admin rights, lab items; '*'
  included) and answers 404 to their routes; user #1 still needs the second factor there.
- Start-up steps and loops in one retried attempt; /ready answers 503 until it ran (R2-3, R2-36). The hourly purges in
  their own task, each in its own transaction and try, batched, backed off, try-locked; the backtest loop's prune and
  reap apart from its claim (R2-33). GET /version; a mark of each shared secret in the start line (R2-8).
- The pending C2-TRACE test moves into the suite, changed to the decided pairing; test_edge's cleanup test follows the
  purges to the housekeeping task. railway.ts declares edge-bff-live as a comment.

