+  | Phase 1 (sessions with an account) | a build before Phase 1 cannot refuse a switch-on session of user #1 | before such a rollback revoke every session `WHERE user_id IS NOT NULL` (R2-1) |
+  | 3d: the Watchlist file split | edge-bff first (it tolerates a missing `radar`), then the publisher | the publisher back before edge-bff |
+
+## 18. Who receives personal data (R2-28; the list the Privacy text states)
+
+The Privacy and Terms text is the user's content, outside this execution (EXEC.md). It states these recipients; a page
+or service that adds one adds its row here in the same change (`tests/test_contract_records.py` fails on a third-party
+host of the server's code or of a resource a page loads that this table does not name).
+
+| Recipient | Host | What it receives | When |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Google Fonts | `fonts.googleapis.com`, `fonts.gstatic.com` | each visitor's IP address and user agent (the Inter font) | every EDGE page, the sign-in and registration pages included, before any sign-in. **Open:** self-host Inter (`font-src 'self'`, no visible change) or keep it and state it |
+| Resend | `api.resend.com` | every email address EDGE writes to and each email's body (codes, notices) | each registration, code, reset and notice (the live site, switch on) |
+| The market-file bucket (Railway storage) | `*.t3.storageapi.dev` | the visitor's IP address and the object keys of presigned downloads | the Terminal, Backtest and Watchlist pages' file downloads; with 3c a capped principal gets cuts and reference copies through edge-bff instead |
+| Have I Been Pwned (Pwned Passwords) | `api.pwnedpasswords.com` | the first 5 hexadecimal characters of the password's SHA-1 (k-anonymity; not personal data) | each new password (registration, reset, change) |
+| Railway | the hosting | every request, the logs (no secret, codes masked) and the database | always |
+| OpenRouter and its model providers (market-ai-orc) | through Orc | the admin's questions and the data the AI reads | the Monitor, admin only (D1); no user's question while the AI is admin-only |
+| A payment provider (Phase 5) | to be named | the order, the amount and the payer's details | when payment opens |
